(1128934, 135276, 2741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kylie:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done new perspective!!!!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is not a new perspective. This angle is a very popular here in NYC. They sell tons of these on the street.<br/> <br/>But yes, this shot is definitely the best of the other entries. Good job.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nazgul:</b></div><hr/><i> Blurry! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Where?  This image is sharp. Just look at the cables. Focus is excellent.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-24 11:20:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Kylie: Well done new perspective!!!!!   This is not a new perspective. This angle is a very popular here in NYC. They sell tons of these on the street. But yes, this shot is definitely the best of the other entries. Good job. Originally posted by Nazgul: Blurry!   Where?  This image is sharp. Just look at the cables. Focus is excellent.', '2005-01-24 10:41:34.000000', '2005-01-24 11:20:15.000000', 0),
(1128937, 137006, 22734, '<td valign="top">"One eye commentator":<br/>Jon you hve that natural knack, that deftly eye and plenty of talent to milk out the goodness and beauty of an image. You are certainly an exception when it comes to talent. Congrats for your 4th place finish with this coruscating image. A definte wall hanger. Good luck with your trade and hope you get published beyond your dreams. You are truly one of my favs photographer.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-24 10:45:27.</i></td>', '"One eye commentator":Jon you hve that natural knack, that deftly eye and plenty of talent to milk out the goodness and beauty of an image. You are certainly an exception when it comes to talent. Congrats for your 4th place finish with this coruscating image. A definte wall hanger. Good luck with your trade and hope you get published beyond your dreams. You are truly one of my favs photographer.', '2005-01-24 10:44:59.000000', '2005-01-24 10:45:27.000000', 0),
(1128941, 137158, 22734, '<td valign="top">"One eye commentator":<br/>Alan: congratulations on your 5th placing. This image is very special because its spacial content gives me the feeling that i am a bird soaring and looking down. All I can say, as jaw slowly drops, is unbelievable!</td>', '"One eye commentator":Alan: congratulations on your 5th placing. This image is very special because its spacial content gives me the feeling that i am a bird soaring and looking down. All I can say, as jaw slowly drops, is unbelievable!', '2005-01-24 10:48:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1128942, 137012, 25486, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments: <br/> <br/>laurielblack <br/>I wasn''t sure about the "glow" myself but I couldn''t think of anything else to detract from the otherwise blown out sky. <br/> <br/>ubique <br/>Not the first one to have compared it to snails :-) <br/> <br/>autool <br/>I shall pay more attention next time to the cropping. <br/> <br/>asij <br/>Thanks, glad you liked it. <br/> <br/>claudia26 <br/>I thought it was a bit different and hoped that would help in the voting. <br/> <br/>tazza <br/>Glad you liked it, it is a great building. My shot doesn''t convey the scale of it I don''t think, but if you look in my portfolio there are some close up shots which will give you an idea of the size. <br/> <br/>geghis <br/>The crop is a bit tight on the bottom you''re right. There is a very large warehouse type building below it and the steel corrugated roof is just below and I had to crop it out. <br/> <br/>SandyP <br/>It is interesting architecture, glad you liked it. <br/> <br/>fredandaud <br/>It was about 09:30 Sunday morning just as the market was being setup. Are you from the NE?<br/> <br/>Edited for spelling!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-24 10:49:42.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments:  laurielblack I wasn''t sure about the "glow" myself but I couldn''t think of anything else to detract from the otherwise blown out sky.  ubique Not the first one to have compared it to snails :-)  autool I shall pay more attention next time to the cropping.  asij Thanks, glad you liked it.  claudia26 I thought it was a bit different and hoped that would help in the voting.  tazza Glad you liked it, it is a great building. My shot doesn''t convey the scale of it I don''t think, but if you look in my portfolio there are some close up shots which will give you an idea of the size.  geghis The crop is a bit tight on the bottom you''re right. There is a very large warehouse type building below it and the steel corrugated roof is just below and I had to crop it out.  SandyP It is interesting architecture, glad you liked it.  fredandaud It was about 09:30 Sunday morning just as the market was being setup. Are you from the NE? Edited for spelling!', '2005-01-24 10:48:09.000000', '2005-01-24 10:49:42.000000', 0),
